# Semantic Growth Implementation Status

Updated: 2026-08-05

## Current stage

Stage 1 (LangGraph minimum durable human-review loop) is complete.

Implemented:

- Independent `src/semantic_growth` orchestration package and `GrowthState`.
- Durable runs, opportunities, step records, candidate links, and PostgreSQL checkpoints.
- `load_scope -> discover_opportunity -> persist_pending_candidate -> human_review` graph.
- Stage-1 mock candidates in the existing `semantic_claim_candidates` pool.
- Human interrupt plus `Command(resume=...)` recovery.
- Create, state, and resume APIs under `/rag/growth-runs`.
- Idempotent opportunity, candidate, and link writes.

## Acceptance evidence

- Unit and semantic regression tests: 17 passed.
- Three separate processes created, reloaded, and resumed one persisted graph.
- Different threads remained isolated and a wrong persisted `thread_id` was rejected.
- `fastapi_travel` restarted successfully.
- HTTP create/state/resume returned 200; wrong-thread resume returned 409.
- Audit runs retained: `growth-stage1-it-20260805-a`, `growth-stage1-http-20260805-a`.

## API and boundary

- `POST /rag/growth-runs`
- `GET /rag/growth-runs/{growth_run_id}`
- `POST /rag/growth-runs/{growth_run_id}/resume`

Stage 1 supports accept, modify, and reject. Retry loops and formal publication are later stages.

## Next stage

Stage 2 replaces mock nodes with adapters over the existing text completion chain. Acceptance: select one domain, discover 10 real template gaps, and persist reviewable candidates through the existing pool.

## Existing environment warnings

The shared environment already reports `langgraph-prebuilt`/`langchain-core`, LLaMA Factory/NumPy, requests, and Pydantic compatibility warnings. Stage 1 passed imports, tests, startup, PostgreSQL persistence, and HTTP acceptance. Do not upgrade the shared model environment during Stage 2 without a separate compatibility pass.
